/-!
# ArithS.Necessitation.Layout — the three layout producers: copy-in, chains, identification

`M4_BOUNDED_HBL/DESIGN_fragments.md` §3.3–3.5, as Σ₁ step-list producers against the step
language of `Chain.lean` and the list infrastructure of `Describe.lean` Part 0, each with its
Π₁ applicability theorem in the `describeT_ok` shape (`ListOK ∧ NoDrop ∧ HornOnly ∧ shiftsV = count
∧ the produced facts ∈ finalCtx`, facts stated as canonical codes at explicit indices) and its
length; the cost follows from `costSum_le_of_hornOnly` (every list here is Horn-only).

## Part 1 — the layout table (GENERATED by the session script `gen_layout1.py`)

`layoutRows := walkRows ++ layoutExtraRows` — the 40 walk rows at their indices followed by the
46 rows the producers use (copy-in `eqTotal`/`eqRefl`/`eqSymm`/`eqTrans`/`cong*`, identification
`eqOf*`, `subsetAntisymm`, the chain rows `*C` of `Lib/Frag.lean` group K), `lIdx_<row> = 40 + k`;
`LayoutTable tbl` (implies `WalkTable tbl`), `exists_layoutTable`; the piece table `layoutPieces`
extends `walkPieces` entrywise (`mkStep_layoutPieces_lt`), so the walk's `ok_<row>` lemmas
transfer; per row `lmk_<row>`, `layoutTable_<row>`, `ltag_<row>`, `lok_<row>`.

## Part 2 — copy-in (`copySteps`, §3.3)

A FACT TAG `⟪kind, args⟫` names one fact of the source object's dossier by its kind (`0` pi, `1`
and, `2` or, `3` all, `4` exs, `5` rel, `6` nrel, `7` verum, `8` falsum, `9` len, `10` mem, `11`
tpi, `12` func, `13` bvar, `14` fvar, `15` tlen, `16` adj, `17` tvpi, `18` utvpi) and the OTHER
witnesses of that fact (closed terms in the frame BEFORE the copy; for the shape facts also the
NEW children, whose identification `eqFactB child' child` is assumed in context). `copySteps W i T`
= `sIntroFact eqTotal [^&i]` (the fresh `&0` with `eqFactB &0 &(i+1)`, everything shifted once)
followed, per tag, by the congruence step(s) (`cong<kind>`, plus the `.sigma → .pi` bridge row of
the walk for the four formation kinds). `copySteps_ok`: under `TagOK` for every tag (kind `< 19`,
witnesses closed with shifted length `≤ E`, the tag's antecedents in `Γ`), the list is applicable,
Horn-only, shifts exactly once, and its final context holds `eqFactB &0 &(i+1)` and every
`tagFact` — the copied fact about `&0` with the witnesses shifted.

## Part 3 — chains (`chainSteps`, §3.4)

`chainSteps W xs` for a vector of member terms (frame before the chain): `k` intro steps
`insertTotalC` building `s₁ = insert x₁ 𝟎, …, s_k` (so `s_j` ends at `&(k − j)`), then the
membership facts in one backward pass (`subsetInsertC`/`subsetTransC` for `s_j ⊆ s_k`,
`memInsertSelfC` + `subsetMemC`), the formula-set facts (`emptySubsetC` + `fsetOfSubsetZeroC` for
`𝟎`, then `isFormulaSetInsertC` + `fsetSigmaPiC` per link, needing `piFact 𝟎 x_j` from the dossiers),
and finally `setLenTotalC` for the length object `l_s = &0` (every chain object moves up by one).

## Part 4 — identification (`eqSteps`, §3.5)

Two walk-style dossiers of the SAME code `r` at offsets `i` and `j` (the layout convention: the top
at the offset, the descendants at the walk's relative offsets) yield `eqFactB &i &j` bottom-up by
the injectivity rows `eqOf*` (`eqRefl` on the literal `𝟎` for empty vectors). The producer is a
TEMPLATE computed once per code by the walk's own recursion shape (`TermRec`, a fold from the end,
`UformulaRec1`) and RELOCATED to the two offsets; the dossier is the relocated fact list
(`dossFacts`/`DossierAt`), and `eqSteps_ok` is proved by one template invariant (`TOK`) over terms,
vectors and formulas. The bridge from the walk's final context to `DossierAt` is NOT in this file.
-/

